    {
      "text": "The wings are protected by rain-repellent dust. As a result, this Pokémon can fly about even in rain.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Butterfree has a superior ability to search for delicious honey from flowers. It can even search out, extract, and carry honey from flowers that are blooming over six miles from its nest.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Butterfree has a superior ability to search for delicious honey from flowers. It can even search out, extract, and carry honey from flowers that are blooming over six miles from its nest.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Close examination of its large eyes reveals that each eye is composed of a myriad of tiny eyes.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "When attacked by other Pokémon, it defends itself by scattering its poisonous scales and fluttering its wings.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its wings are covered in toxic scales. If it finds bird Pokémon going after Caterpie, Butterfree sprinkles its scales on them to drive them off.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nectar from pretty flowers is its favorite food. In fields of flowers, it has heated battles with Cutiefly for territory.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its wings, covered with poisonous powder, repel water. This allows it to fly in the rain.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its wings, covered with poisonous powder, repel water. This allows it to fly in the rain.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    },
    {
      "text": "In battle, it flaps its wings at great speed to release highly toxic dust into the air.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "It collects honey every day. It rubs honey onto the hairs on its legs to carry it back to its nest.",
      "version": "shield"
